  "question": {
    "text": "A solid sphere of uniform density and radius <math><mi>r</mi></math> applies a gravitational force of attraction equal to <math><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math>on a particle placed at <math><mi>P</mi></math>, distance <math><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math> from the centre <math><mi>O</mi></math> of the sphere. A spherical cavity of the radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> is now made in the sphere as shown in the figure. The sphere with cavity now applied a gravitational force <math><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> on the same particle placed at <math><mi>P</mi></math>. The ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math> will be<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0028535_Question.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 105px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
